<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qadi Isa Savaji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1491</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qadi">Qadi</a> Isa Savaji was a judge and leading minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruler Ya'qub (r. 1478–1490). He attempted a fiscal reform that aimed to revoke hereditary tax exemptions, known as soyurghal, and to bring taxation closer to Islamic law. The reform provoked strong opposition from the military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> and religious notables, and after Ya'qub's death Qadi Isa was executed and his reforms abandoned.</p></div>
